@abstract{
In 1930, the iris dataset was introduced by the British statistician and
biologist Ronald Fisher. The dataset consists of 150 samples of iris flowers,
with 50 samples from each of three species: Iris setosa, Iris versicolor, and
Iris virginica. We recreate his analysis in this report.
}

> Introduction

The iris is a famous dataset in the field of machine learning and statistics. It
consists of 150 samples from three species of iris flowers (Iris setosa, Iris
versicolor, and Iris virginica). Each sample has four features: sepal length,
sepal width, petal length, and petal width. The dataset is widely used for
classification tasks and serves as a benchmark for various machine learning
algorithms.


